The '''Ever-Flowing Icepack''' is a [[Contraption|contraption]] that functions as an icepack that always stays cold.

==Description (Contraption)==
[[Coco]]'s thought process behind making this contraption is to create an icepack that stays cool forever, taking inspiration from the cool, flowing water from rivers and streams.{{Ref|m|32|29}} The contraption's outward appearance isn't all that different from a typical icepack, apart from the way it moves and sounds as water sloshes around inside of it. Qifrey's first impression of it is that of "some manner of fidgeting icepack."{{Ref|m|36|9}}

==Description (Casting Seal)==
Coco's initial attempt at creating the Casting Seal for this contraption results in water rapidly and sporadically spinning above the seal. The seal is partially shown to include several angled Signs of [[Signs#Columns|Columns]]. The signs are presumably arranged in a circle and surrounding a central Sigil of [[Sigils#Water|Water]].

When [[Olruggio]] steps in to lend a hand, he draws a singular, small Sign of Columns opposite to a standard Water Sigil. In doing so, the water stills into the shape of a thin disc floating above the seal. When Coco gives it another try, Olruggio advises her to keep the sign small, in the center and adjust it to get the flow right.{{Ref|m|32|29}}
